<figure><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20260910-notebooks.jpg" alt="3 notebooks on my desk"></figure><p>This is only 3 out of the five (soon to be 6<sup class="footnote-ref"><a href="https://baty.net/posts/2026/09/i-just-need-to-pick-a-notebook-already/#fn1" id="fnref1">[1]</a></sup>) notebooks I use regularly. I don't use all of them because I <em>need</em> them. I use them because I can't decide which notebook to use for which purpose.</p>
<!-- more -->
<p>In the photo are:</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://shop.travelerscompanyusa.com/products/travelers-notebook-brown">Traveler's Notebook</a></strong>. This is nice for when I want to have options. I can throw all sorts of inserts in there, and I do. The cover feels great and has worn nicely.</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://fieldnotesbrand.com/">Field Notes</a></strong>. I've carried a little Field Notes notebook for a long time. I'm not always sure why, as I seldom actually write anything in them. It's comforting to know it's there, though. Maybe one day I'll have a &quot;thought or idea&quot; while I'm out and about and I'll be ready.</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://baronfig.com/products/confidant-hardcover-notebook">Baronfig Confidant Hardcover Notebook</a></strong>. My first Baronfig. It's nice, but I'm not sure I prefer it to my usual Leuchtturm. I use it for tasks, lists, etc. It's my version of a &quot;bullet journal&quot;.</p>
<p>Others are: a Leuchtturm for a kind of scrapbook where I paste photos, receipts, etc. and write short notes about them. The other is a Midori MD Notebook, which is supposed to be a journal/diary. It would be, but I have too many other places to write things, so this one is only used occasionally. See what I mean?</p>
<figure>
<img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20260910-stack-of-notebooks.jpg" alt="A stack of notebooks" />
<figcaption>These are just the ones I can reach from my desk</figcaption>
</figure>
<p>I've been here a few times. See <a href="https://archive.baty.net/2016/three-notebooks/">Three Notebooks</a> from 2016.</p>
<p>Just like with blogs, I'd prefer to have just one notebook for everything, but I'm not a person who can do that, apparently.</p>
